        "text": "<https://algot.org/> \u2014 a research visual, by-demonstration (aka code while seeing concrete values :cake:), language operating on graphs.  Papers largely closed-access but <https://people.inf.ethz.ch/~sverrirt/publications/|preprints here>.\nI find it a bit hard to imagine how one uses it from screenshots, and ~didn't find videos / lectures?~ OK here's a (silent) demo: <https://vimeo.com/729159376>\n\nIn some ways similar to <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4rLGHBio5UI|Subsequently> in de-ambiguating user intent by \"demonstration\" not being \"say the result\" but \"pick an action\".",
